// Mission 05: the KQL I ran in the shared Sentinel workspace (log-hamilton) -> Logs
// Times in UTC. This workspace collects Security events from the domain controller
// (DC01), shared across the whole class -- so results here are domain-wide, not just
// my own seat, unless filtered down.

// Step 1: is the DC reporting into this workspace?
Heartbeat
| where Computer has "DC01"
| summarize LastSeen = max(TimeGenerated)

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Step 2: find my own Kerberoasting ticket request (4769) at the source
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Event 4769 (Kerberos Service Ticket Requested) packs its useful fields into the
// EventData column as a small XML document rather than flat SecurityEvent columns.
// Reusable unpack pattern (the new skill this mission is built around):
//
//   SecurityEvent
//   | where EventID == 4769
//   | extend Parsed = parse_xml(EventData).EventData.Data
//   | mv-expand Parsed
//   | extend Name = tostring(Parsed["@Name"]), Value = tostring(Parsed["#text"])
//   | summarize Fields = make_bag(pack(Name, Value)) by TimeGenerated, EventRecordId
//   | evaluate bag_unpack(Fields)
//
// Field semantics (confirmed empirically, not obvious from the names): on a 4769,
// TargetUserName is the REQUESTING account, ServiceName is the TARGETED account/SPN
// -- the opposite direction from how these names work on a 4624 logon event.
// Filtering on TargetUserName has "svc-app58" surfaces 495 unrelated rows: routine
// AES256 (0x12) machine-ticket renewals from the still-firing Mission 4
// M4-SvcApp58-Persistence scheduled task (svc-app58 as ticket *owner*, not target).
// The correct filter for "someone requested a ticket targeting svc-app58" is
// ServiceName has "svc-app58".

SecurityEvent
| where TimeGenerated > ago(90d)
| where EventID == 4769
| where Computer has "DC01"
| extend Parsed = parse_xml(EventData).EventData.Data
| mv-expand Parsed
| extend Name = tostring(Parsed["@Name"]), Value = tostring(Parsed["#text"])
| summarize Fields = make_bag(pack(Name, Value)) by TimeGenerated, EventRecordId
| evaluate bag_unpack(Fields)
| where ServiceName has "svc-app58"
| project TimeGenerated, TargetUserName, ServiceName, TicketEncryptionType, IpAddress
| order by TimeGenerated asc

// Result: exactly one row -- mustafa@HAMILTON.CORP requesting a ticket for
// svc-app58, 2026-11-05 11:36:38.661 UTC, TicketEncryptionType 0x17 (RC4),
// IpAddress ::ffff:10.50.0.1 (the Tailscale gateway address, same masking pattern
// observed throughout Mission 4). This is my own Mission 4 Part 2 Kerberoast, found
// at the DC instead of reasoned about.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Step 3: why it stands out -- encryption type across the whole domain
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
SecurityEvent
| where TimeGenerated > ago(90d)
| where EventID == 4769
| where Computer has "DC01"
| extend Parsed = parse_xml(EventData).EventData.Data
| mv-expand Parsed
| extend Name = tostring(Parsed["@Name"]), Value = tostring(Parsed["#text"])
| summarize Fields = make_bag(pack(Name, Value)) by TimeGenerated, EventRecordId
| evaluate bag_unpack(Fields)
| summarize Count=count(), Accounts=dcount(TargetUserName), Services=dcount(ServiceName) by TicketEncryptionType
| order by Count desc

// Result: 8,132 AES256 (0x12) events across 41 accounts / 20 services (routine,
// 99.8% of all traffic) vs. 16 RC4 (0x17) events across 7 accounts / 8 services
// (0.2%) -- the rare, distinguishing signal. Matches Mission 4 Part 2's finding
// that the cracked ticket was "etype 23" (decimal for RC4-HMAC = hex 0x17).
// This is the heart of the detection rule: TicketEncryptionType == "0x17" on a
// service-ticket request is abnormal enough in this domain to hunt on directly.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Step 4: replay + ingestion delay
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Replayed only the ticket-request step (own seat's svc-app58, no cracking) from
// my own laptop at ~2026-11-09 11:19 UTC via the same Impacket command as Mission 4
// Part 2's Step 6. Then re-ran the Step 2 query narrowed to the last 30 minutes:

SecurityEvent
| where TimeGenerated > ago(30m)
| where EventID == 4769
| where Computer has "DC01"
| extend Parsed = parse_xml(EventData).EventData.Data
| mv-expand Parsed
| extend Name = tostring(Parsed["@Name"]), Value = tostring(Parsed["#text"])
| summarize Fields = make_bag(pack(Name, Value)) by TimeGenerated, EventRecordId
| evaluate bag_unpack(Fields)
| where ServiceName has "svc-app58"
| project TimeGenerated, TargetUserName, ServiceName, TicketEncryptionType, IpAddress
| order by TimeGenerated desc

// Result: TimeGenerated 2026-11-09 11:19:03.546 UTC, mustafa@HAMILTON.CORP ->
// svc-app58, 0x17 (RC4), ::ffff:10.50.0.1 (Tailscale gateway again). The event was
// already queryable ~25-30s after the replay -- the very first query against the
// workspace found it. Ingestion delay: well under a minute. This justifies a
// 5-minute rule frequency with a lookback slightly longer than 5 minutes (not
// exactly equal -- avoids missing an event that lands right at the query-window
// boundary, per the brief's warning).

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Step 5: generalize to a detection query, review false positives
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// All 21 RC4 (0x17) events over the 90-day window, no seat/account/time filter --
// reviewed to check for false positives before generalizing.
SecurityEvent
| where TimeGenerated > ago(90d)
| where EventID == 4769
| where Computer has "DC01"
| extend Parsed = parse_xml(EventData).EventData.Data
| mv-expand Parsed
| extend Name = tostring(Parsed["@Name"]), Value = tostring(Parsed["#text"])
| summarize Fields = make_bag(pack(Name, Value)) by TimeGenerated, EventRecordId
| evaluate bag_unpack(Fields)
| where TicketEncryptionType == "0x17"
| project TimeGenerated, TargetUserName, ServiceName, IpAddress
| order by TimeGenerated asc

// Result: 21 rows, all human accounts requesting svc-appNN tickets. Zero computer
// accounts ($ suffix), zero krbtgt -- RC4 alone is a clean signal in this domain
// with no observed false positives. Still added defensive exclusions below rather
// than relying on that holding forever.

// Generalized detection query -- this is what the Step 6 analytics rule runs.
// Dropped every self-specific filter (seat/account/time); kept only the
// encryption-type signal; excluded computer accounts and krbtgt defensively
// (legitimate in some domains even though not observed here).
SecurityEvent
| where EventID == 4769
| where Computer has "DC01"
| extend Parsed = parse_xml(EventData).EventData.Data
| mv-expand Parsed
| extend Name = tostring(Parsed["@Name"]), Value = tostring(Parsed["#text"])
| summarize Fields = make_bag(pack(Name, Value)) by TimeGenerated, EventRecordId
| evaluate bag_unpack(Fields)
| where TicketEncryptionType == "0x17"
| where TargetUserName !endswith "$"
| where TargetUserName != "krbtgt"
| project TimeGenerated, TargetUserName, ServiceName, IpAddress, TicketEncryptionType

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Step 6: final analytics rule query (as saved in the "L58 - RC4 Kerberos
// service ticket request (Kerberoasting)" scheduled rule)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The Step 5 query, as typed into the rule wizard's "Set rule logic" editor,
// tripped its static validator: 'where' operator: Failed to resolve column
// or scalar expression named 'TicketEncryptionType' (and, once patched,
// the same for TargetUserName). "View query results" proved the query runs
// correctly regardless (13 rows, matching the manual hunt) -- the editor's
// analyzer can't statically infer columns produced dynamically by
// `evaluate bag_unpack(...)`. Unlike the earlier cosmetic version of this
// warning seen during ad-hoc hunting, the wizard's Review + create step
// actually blocks saving on it. Fix: wrap each bag_unpack-produced column
// used downstream in column_ifexists("ColumnName", "") right after
// bag_unpack -- its return type is statically known, so the analyzer stops
// trying to resolve the dynamic column by name.
SecurityEvent
| where EventID == 4769
| where Computer has "DC01"
| extend Parsed = parse_xml(EventData).EventData.Data
| mv-expand Parsed
| extend Name = tostring(Parsed["@Name"]), Value = tostring(Parsed["#text"])
| summarize Fields = make_bag(pack(Name, Value)) by TimeGenerated, EventRecordId
| evaluate bag_unpack(Fields)
| extend TicketEncryptionType = tostring(column_ifexists("TicketEncryptionType", "")), TargetUserName = tostring(column_ifexists("TargetUserName", "")), ServiceName = tostring(column_ifexists("ServiceName", "")), IpAddress = tostring(column_ifexists("IpAddress", ""))
| where TicketEncryptionType == "0x17"
| where TargetUserName !endswith "$"
| where TargetUserName != "krbtgt"
| project TimeGenerated, TargetUserName, ServiceName, IpAddress, TicketEncryptionType

// Rule settings: Severity High, MITRE T1558.003 (Kerberoasting). Run every
// 5 minutes, lookback 10 minutes (not equal -- avoids missing an event that
// lands right at the query-window boundary; justified by Step 4's measured
// <1 minute ingestion delay). Alert threshold: results > 0, "trigger an
// alert for each event" (not grouped). Entity mapping: Account/FullName ->
// TargetUserName, IP/Address -> IpAddress.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Step 7: proof-of-fire -- replayed svc-app58 again, let the scheduled rule
// (not an ad-hoc query) pick it up on its own cadence
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Raw event landed at 2026-11-09 11:19:03.546 UTC. Incident #3050/#3052
// ("L58 - RC4 Kerberos service ticket request (Kerberoasting)") shows a
// timeline entry "9 Nov 15:02:22 ... Detected by Microsoft Sentinel ...
// Credential Access" with Entities mustafa@HAMILTON.CORP / ::ffff:10.50.0.1 --
// the incident UI displays UTC+1, confirmed by comparing to a second replay
// at 14:02:22.845 UTC lining up with a "15:02" incident entry. Caught well
// inside the rule's 10-minute lookback.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Step 8: triage -- who else is tripping this (domain-wide, unfiltered) rule
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// The rule has no account filter by design, so it also fires on classmates'
// own Mission 4/5 work. Pulled every RC4 (0x17) ticket request over the last
// 24h, all accounts, to see the full pattern:
SecurityEvent
| where TimeGenerated > ago(24h)
| where EventID == 4769
| where Computer has "DC01"
| extend Parsed = parse_xml(EventData).EventData.Data
| mv-expand Parsed
| extend Name = tostring(Parsed["@Name"]), Value = tostring(Parsed["#text"])
| summarize Fields = make_bag(pack(Name, Value)) by TimeGenerated, EventRecordId
| evaluate bag_unpack(Fields)
| extend TicketEncryptionType = tostring(column_ifexists("TicketEncryptionType", "")), TargetUserName = tostring(column_ifexists("TargetUserName", "")), ServiceName = tostring(column_ifexists("ServiceName", "")), IpAddress = tostring(column_ifexists("IpAddress", ""))
| where TicketEncryptionType == "0x17"
| project TimeGenerated, TargetUserName, ServiceName, IpAddress, TicketEncryptionType
| order by TimeGenerated desc

// Result (17 rows): every requesting account maps to exactly one targeted
// service account, and it's always that student's own seat:
//   mustafa   -> svc-app58  (me, x2: the Step 4 and Step 7 replays)
//   kien      -> svc-app66  (x8, incl. the 13:50:39 UTC event behind
//                            incidents #3045/#3047 -- my rule catching
//                            HIS replay, the Step 8 target)
//   lakshmi   -> svc-app53  (x3)
//   derya     -> svc-app59  (x2)
//   training01 -> svc-app59 (x2, same target as derya -- consistent with
//                            Mission 3's training01 being scoped near that
//                            seat)
// Source IP on every single row: ::ffff:10.50.0.1 (shared Tailscale gateway
// -- no per-student attribution from IP alone, domain-wide).
//
// Judgment: classmate-replay-within-shared-workspace-rules, not an incident.
// Kien's own-seat, steady-cadence, single-target pattern is exactly what
// "everyone Kerberoasting their own seat's service account for this mission"
// looks like from the DC's point of view. Already self-resolved (#3045) by
// Kien. See notes.md Step 8 for the full first-line-analyst triage writeup,
// including the double-alert quirk (#3045 + #3047 for what's apparently the
// same 13:50:39 UTC event -- a lookback-wider-than-interval side effect, not
// a detection gap).
